ows, noting each instance where the value starts with 1. The second table requires similar careful analysis. I'll go through each row, tracking values that begin with the digit 1, ensuring no duplicates are missed. This methodical approach will help me verify the total count and confirm the accuracy of my previous calculation.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_59cfb1d18b7a98b8","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"python3 << 'EOF'\n# Let me verify by counting carefully from the raw data\n\n# First table - extract all numeric cells\n# Based on the table structure in the text\n# Row 2-24 are data rows with values:\n# Year, then 9 columns of data\n\n# Let me verify the first table row by row\ntext = open('/app/resources/treasury_bulletin_1980_05_page_41.txt').read()\nrows = re.findall(r'<tr>(.*?)</tr>', text)\n\nprint(\"=== FIRST TABLE ===\")\nprint(\"Checking first table structure:\")\nprint(f\"Row 1 (headers): {re.findall(r'<t[dh]>([^<]*)</t[dh]>', rows[1])[:10]}\")\nprint(f\"Row 2 (1971): {re.findall(r'<t[dh]>([^<]*)</t[dh]>', rows[2])}\")\n\n# Count first table leading 1s\nfirst_table_count = 0\nfor i in range(2, 25):\n    cells = re.findall(r'<t[dh]>([^<]*)</t[dh]>', rows[i])\n    # Skip first column (row header), process remaining\n    for cell in cells[1:]:\n        cell = cell.strip()\n        cell = re.sub(r'\\d+/', '', cell)\n        cell = cell.rstrip('r').strip()\n        if cell and cell not in ['*', '']:\n            clean = cell.replace(',', '')\n            if clean and clean[0] == '1':\n                first_table_count += 1\n                print(f\"  FT: {cell}\")\n\nprint(f\"\\nFirst table count: {first_table_count}\")\n\nprint(\"\\n=== SECOND TABLE ===\")\n# Second table\nsecond_table_count = 0\nfor i in range(27, 50):\n    cells = re.findall(r'<t[dh]>([^<]*)</t[dh]>', rows[i])\n    for cell in cells[1:]:\n        cell = cell.strip()\n        cell = re.sub(r'\\d+/', '', cell)\n        cell